{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
In the hill coun[C]try of [Dm]Ephraim, between Ra[C]mah [Dm]and Bethel's stones
Sat Debo[C]rah beneath the [Bb]palm [C]while Israel cried [Dm]and [Bb]groaned
Nine hun[F]dred iron char[Dm]iots had [C]kept them [Bb]twenty [Dm]years
The highways lay empty
[C]And travelers kept to the wind[Am]ing trails [Dm]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
She sent for [C]Barak in Nap[Dm]htali and gave him [C]the [Dm]LORD's command
Go, march [C]to Mount Tabor
[Bb]With [C]ten thousand [Dm]at your hand
[Bb]If you go with [C]me, I will go
[Am]I will surely go with you, she [Dm]said
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Awake, [C]awake, [Dm]Deborah
Awake, [C]a[Dm]wake, break into song
[Bb]I will sing to [C]the LORD, I my[Dm]self will sing
I [Bb]will make music [C]to the LORD, the God [Dm]of Israel
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
