{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]The chariots came thun[C]dering across the [Dm]Kishon plain
The earth shook, [C]the heavens poured
The [Bb]clouds [C]poured down wa[Dm]ter
From the heav[Bb]ens they fought
[C]The [Am]river Kishon swept them away
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Dm]Village life [C]in Israel ceased
Un[Bb]til I, Deborah, a[C]rose
Un[Dm]til I a[C]rose, a [Bb]moth[C]er in Is[Dm]rael
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Awake, [C]awake, [Dm]Deborah
Awake, [C]awake, [Dm]break into song
[Bb]I will sing to [C]the LORD, I myself [Dm]will sing
